[Host] Time for a short quiz. Listen and try to answer.

66
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:47,264
[Slow] 7月28日に熊本県で起きた地震では、最大でどのくらいの揺れを観測しましたか。

67
00:11:48,063 --> 00:11:55,384
[Host] Intensity seven, the highest level on Japan's seismic scale, in the cities of Uki and Hikawa.

68
00:11:55,984 --> 00:12:03,399
[Slow] 今、およそ何人が避難所で避難生活を送っていますか。

69
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:09,360
[Host] About nine thousand five hundred people, at more than four hundred shelters.

70
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:40,032
[Host] That's all for today. On July twenty-eighth, a magnitude seven point one earthquake struck Kumamoto Prefecture, with shaking of intensity seven at its strongest. Thirty-four people have died, and about nine thousand five hundred people are staying in shelters amid intense summer heat, while water and power outages continue and the Kyushu bullet train remains suspended. Our thoughts are with everyone affected. Thanks for listening, and see you tomorrow.

71
00:12:40,631 --> 00:12:43,032
[News] また明日。
